# Every Feature Must Be Responsive

The app has a slide-in sidebar drawer on mobile/tablet (`< lg`) and a fixed sidebar on desktop (`lg+`). Every new UI feature must work on all three breakpoints.

## Checklist for every new component or page

- [ ] Tested at mobile (375px), tablet (768px), and desktop (1280px)
- [ ] Page content uses `px-4 py-6 md:px-8 md:py-8`, never fixed `px-8`
- [ ] No fixed widths that would overflow on small screens
- [ ] Button labels hidden on mobile if space is tight: `<span className="hidden sm:inline">Label</span>`
- [ ] Grids use mobile-first columns: `grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3`
- [ ] No hardcoded `-50` tint colors (`bg-emerald-50` etc.) — use `bg-emerald-500/10` instead

## Page layout pattern

```tsx
// ✅ Every page inside AppShell
<div className="px-4 py-6 md:px-8 md:py-8 max-w-5xl">
  ...
</div>
```

## Buttons with labels

```tsx
// ✅ Icon-only on mobile, label on sm+
<Button className="gap-2">
  <Upload className="w-4 h-4" />
  <span className="hidden sm:inline">Upload</span>
</Button>
```

## Grids

```tsx
// ✅
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-3">

// ❌
<div className="grid grid-cols-3 gap-3">
```

## Color classes

```tsx
// ✅ Works in light + dark
"bg-emerald-500/10 text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400"

// ❌ Near-white, invisible in dark mode
"bg-emerald-50 text-emerald-700"
```
